## Decisions locked (unchanged from the plan, plus what this session settled)

- Intent is inferred, in the SAME call as the reply; the trailer comes LAST so reasoning precedes
  the verdict. Auto is the default; Clarify/Edit are overrides.
- **Questions never confirm.** Confirmation fatigue is the failure mode.
- `BeatWriteReason.AuthorApprovedProposal` — NOT `AuthorEdit`. The decision is the author's, the
  words are the model's, and the forever-record must be able to tell them apart.
- Post-write checks are **exact and free only**. No LLM sweep: the obligation extractor measured
  96% false positives, and a sweep firing four spurious findings per edit gets turned off.
- Read Mode's absence of a Discuss panel is a **correctness property**, not layout.
- `EditSessionService` is read, never started — `StartSessionAsync` evicts other auto-sessions.
- Description is **never** regenerated from prose (it would make the intent check tautological);
  EventSummary is regenerated freely.

## HARD gotchas (do not rediscover)

- **The author redeploys, not me.** A local build changes nothing.
- **`@page.Text` in Razor markup is parsed as the `@page` directive.** Name the loop variable
  anything else.
- **`@ref` needs an assignable location** — `itemRefs[index]` over an array, not a dictionary.
- **`@{ }` inside an existing Razor code block is a parse error.**
- **`prose.cmd` + a heredoc in one Bash call DEADLOCKS.** Always `< /dev/null`.
- **Every book-touching method must `SetFlowUniverse` first.**
- **All JS interop through a try/catch helper** — an unhandled `JSException` kills the circuit.
- The 5 failing tests are pre-existing (`WorldState*`, `Snapshot*`). Verified at HEAD. Leave them.

